{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reingoldTilfordLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The root is at (0, 0) and a vertex at depth d has y = d. Children are placed left to right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"text":" order, vertices at one depth at least 1 apart along each subtree’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contour, and every parent centred over its first and last child. Where two subtrees had to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be pushed apart, the smaller subtrees between them are spaced evenly (Walker’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"improvement), so a mirrored tree draws as the reflection of the drawing and isomorphic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subtrees are drawn identically up to translation. Coordinates are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":" arithmetic:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"separations and centring alone give multiples of a power of ½, which are exact, but the even","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spacing divides a shift by the number of gaps it is spread over, so values such as ±5\/6","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"occur and are rounded (and a mirrored tree’s drawing then matches the reflection only to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rounding).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reingold and Tilford, “Tidier drawings of trees”, IEEE Transactions on Software"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Engineering SE-7(2), 1981."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Walker, “A node-positioning algorithm for general trees”, Software: Practice and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Experience 20(7), 1990.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Buchheim, Jünger and Leipert, “Improving Walker’s algorithm to run in linear time”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Graph Drawing (GD 2002), LNCS 2528, 2002.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n) time and memory, with no recursion."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Trees\/RootedTree"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/ReingoldTilfordLayout.swift#L37"},"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"Trees","title":"reingoldTilfordLayout()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reingoldTilfordLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier